    "result_text": "Green. I agreed with the finding and applied it.\n\n## What I changed\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a documented derived getter `getMembershipNumber()` next to its siblings (`getCheckDigit()`, `getMembershipLevel()`, etc.), formatting `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` and null-guarding when either `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is unset.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 collapsed the audit block back to a single plain logging call that reads `owner.getMembershipNumber()`, matching how the sibling `owner.getMembershipLevel()` is already logged right beside it.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** (bonus, same rationale) \u2014 the mapper's `addMembershipNumber` held a duplicate copy of the exact same formatting logic. I pointed it at the new getter so the derivation now lives in one place. Behaviour is identical: the mapper previously left the DTO field null when either source field was missing, and the getter returns null in precisely those cases.\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw clean test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` still passes. The AUDIT line is unchanged in output (e.g. `... membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`), and the API DTO's `membershipNumber` is unchanged since both now flow through the same getter.",
